          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "zhídá is built from zhí 'straight' and dá 'to get through', both inherited from Middle Chinese, drik and dat (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'upright' and the second 'to reach through'."
            }
