              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "进入 (jìnrù) is built from 进 'to go forward' and 入 (rù) 'to go in', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tsinH and nyip (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the first 'forward' and the second 'within' and 'to take in'."
